Why Reshape?

Original MNIST shape:

(60000,28,28)

CNN expects:

(batch,height,width,channels)

So we convert into:

(60000,28,28,1)

where:

1

means grayscale channel.

note:

-1

means:

“Automatically calculate number of images.”

NumPy figures it out automatically.

Since total images are 60000:

-1 → 60000


# reshape to add channel dimension
X_train = X_train.reshape(-1,28,28,1)
X_test = X_test.reshape(-1,28,28,1)
     
